# Authority

`data/` is the source of truth for cards, scenarios and rules text. Where each file came from is in `data/sources.json`; where a source was wrong is in `data/overrides.json`, with a reason. Change data by changing the source adapter, the normalizer, the templates or an override, then `pnpm data:build`. Do not hand-edit generated files.

The MEC109 booklet and the quest card win on a rule. The core-set Learn to Play wins on the ordinary round. The Rules Reference wins on definitions. All three are in `data/rules/` and split into rule ids in `data/rules/entries.json`; code and tests name the rule ids they implement. `docs/brief.md` wins on product shape. `docs/architecture.md` wins on how the code is split.

A rule change updates `docs/brief.md` in the same change. Do not commit `catalog.db`, card scans or PDFs. Card text and rules text live in `data/` on purpose.

Implementing a phase is `/implementer`. Reviewing a diff is `/reviewer`. Reviewing screens is `/ux`. Writing effect records for lines no template reads is `effect-author`. Phase status is `docs/phases/STATUS.md`.
